1.2.0 (2026-11-28):
- Edit dialog: new setting "Labels" – descriptions in Polish for a Polish system, English for all others,
  or chosen by hand (English / Polski); only the descriptions change, fields and values stay the same

1.1.0 (2026-11-25):
- Variable picker uses the native global/flow selector, incl. context stores (e.g. persistent "file" store)
- One value field with a type picker: string, integer, float, boolean, JSON (with editor), none
- Fixed: incoming msg.payload was handled wrongly (text failed as JSON, numbers threw an error)
- Incoming plain values are converted to the chosen type, objects are stored as a copy,
  the rest of the message is passed through
- "Emit on init" sends the converted value (and msg.topic = variable name)
- Errors are passed to a Catch node; the start-up timer is cleared on redeploy
- New modern edit dialog (sections, live summary, spinners, validation), palette category "AFYA",
  Font Awesome icon, English UI with English + Polish help
- Short, consistent node status (value · time)
- MIT license, Node-RED >= 3.0, Node.js >= 18, unit tests (`npm test`)

1.0.6:
- engines, readme

1.0.0 – 1.0.5:
- first versions: typed global / flow variables, emit on init
